iving them experiences  they've never had taking them places  giving them access to all kinds of  mind-blowing experiences sure I've made  all of  possible I think the person that has a  toughest especially if in today's world  I hope it changes before you guys become  CEOs is if you're married to somebody  like me how do you cope with it it's not  easy it is not easy because you go to a  party or a dinner I go with my husband  and we walk in and at the end of dinner  see him again so for the three hours  that we're at the dinner been on the  same table I don't know where he is  I'm talking to all kinds of people and  if I don't people say she's too  standoffish so I'm shaking hands taking  pictures and the end of dinner I'm  looking fun because he's my ride home  he looks at me and he goes why do I come  to the event because I don't even enjoy  it I have to dress up like a penguin you  know put on his black tie he said why am  i coming to these events I go because I  knew married me I realized that maybe  put it the other way women always  accepted it you know the same thing  happened to women too when they were  wives they just accepted it because  Society said that's the norm for the  woman to just be nice smile and chitchat  with some other women about coupons and  kids but for men they didn't do that I  mean other times I give you we go to  dinners and I'm sitting between two men  who might be world leaders and having  the time of my life having a great  conversation my husband meanwhile is  sitting between two women were all great  people but they have nothing of interest  to him so he's not making up  conversation to have with him he does a  fantastic job I mean this is I married a  keeper I mean he does a great job but I  tell you I would have a tough time being  married to me there's not easy it is not  easy well at least on your children my  daughter often says she's grateful that  I raised her with such low standards  because she doesn't have to feel guilty  when she goes and has her career  so just think about it that way so let  us return to business I'm gonna ask one  more question then we'll open the floor  for a little bit of time so we're in a  recession I see very happily you've  hired some of my students I'm just very  pleased with that  how how is how is the recession  affecting your businesses you're in a  wide range of different businesses  restaurants beverage a little in Watsons  long time lots of lots of stuff freedom  all kinds of things so how is it  affecting different pieces there's no  question that in the developed world and  I say Western Europe Eastern Europe and  North America we are in a tremendous  downtown there's no question about it  any which way you look at it it's  impacting consumers in a significant way  there's an age of thrift people are  afraid to spend money and people are  being very careful about what they shop  for and where they shop for and when  they shop we've never seen people make  lists for groceries as they do now  everything is a planned purchase in the  past they'd go to a single grocery store  and buy whatever they wanted now they  are willing to make three grocery store  trips to even get the best value so  pricing is going to be very critical the  other thing is being very carefully  watched us if somebody wants to spend $5  on beverages not $5.99 or $6.99 as they  used to before they mentally say I'm  going to spend $5.00 on beverages so how  you do price pack in architecture to  make sure you give them the right  package size for certain dollar outlay  is becoming a more important factor than  just saying what's the price of a  24-pack beverage package so we have to  think differently about the consumer and  how they shop when they get their  paycheck versus the middle of the month  or the week after the paycheck the  patterns are totally different so how  you promote and deal in the different  windows has to change now the good news  is  whether the economy's u