e I go to Washington we have  dinner with the president tonight but  Te'o's they're talking with us all the  time all the time I mean last night we  had a wonderful dinner with Peter Orszag  the head of the Office of Management  budget going through pieces on the  budget so being a CEO today  Washington's very very open to our ideas  the issue is whatever ideas CEOs give  politically can you sell it we've never  seen such a partisan environment so  politically can you sell it so the big  question is it's not the ideas it's how  do you get Washington to accept it and  act on it and I think they like this is  where democracy works against us so yeah  but you know again as you remember it is  one of the things we've always done is  to seriously the public process as well  as the nonprofit and the for-profit  world and I think these days seems like  that's even more important
 

